\section{Introduction}
Transitioning from DigitalOcean App Platform to a \textbf{Droplet} provides full control over the environment and allows us to run MySQL, Nginx, and PHP within our student credits without the overhead of Managed Database costs.

\section{Phase 1: Provisioning the Droplet}
1. \textbf{Create Droplet:} Choose \textbf{Ubuntu 24.04 LTS}.
2. \textbf{Plan:} Basic Plan $\rightarrow$ Regular Intel $\rightarrow$ \$6/month (covered by \$200 credits).
3. \textbf{Authentication:} Use \textbf{SSH Keys} (highly recommended over passwords).
4. \textbf{Firewall:} Enable "Monitoring" and ensure SSH (22), HTTP (80), and HTTPS (443) are allowed.

\section{Phase 2: Server Environment Setup (LEMP)}
Once connected via SSH (\texttt{ssh root@your\_ip}), run:

\subsection{System Update \& Essentials}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
sudo apt install -y git curl unzip zip nginx supervisor
\end{lstlisting}

\subsection{PHP 8.3 Installation}
Matches the requirement in \texttt{composer.json}.
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
sudo add-apt-repository ppa:ondrej/php -y
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y php8.3-fpm php8.3-mysql php8.3-mbstring php8.3-xml php8.3-bcmath php8.3-curl php8.3-zip php8.3-intl
\end{lstlisting}

\subsection{Database Setup (MySQL)}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
sudo apt install -y mysql-server
sudo mysql_secure_installation
# Create DB:
sudo mysql -u root -e "CREATE DATABASE smartshop; CREATE USER 'luwi'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'secure_password'; GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON smartshop.* TO 'luwi'@'localhost'; FLUSH PRIVILEGES;"
\end{lstlisting}

\section{Phase 3: Application Deployment}

\subsection{Cloning \& Permissions}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
cd /var/www
sudo git clone https://github.com/yourusername/e-commerce-platform.git smartshop
sudo chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/smartshop
sudo chmod -R 775 /var/www/smartshop/storage /var/www/smartshop/bootstrap/cache
\end{lstlisting}

\subsection{Composer \& Dependencies}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
curl -sS https://getcomposer.org/installer | php
sudo mv composer.phar /usr/local/bin/composer
cd /var/www/smartshop
composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader
\end{lstlisting}

\subsection{Environment Configuration}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env:
# APP_ENV=production
# APP_DEBUG=false
# DB_DATABASE=smartshop
# DB_USERNAME=luwi
# DB_PASSWORD=secure_password
php artisan key:generate
php artisan migrate --force
\end{lstlisting}

\section{Phase 4: Nginx & SSL Configuration}
1. Create config: \texttt{sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/smartshop}
2. Link it: \texttt{sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/smartshop /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/}
3. Install SSL:
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
sudo apt install -y certbot python3-certbot-nginx
sudo certbot --nginx -d smartshop-luwi.tech
\end{lstlisting}

\section{Phase 5: Performance & Maintenance}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Queue Management:} Configure Supervisor to run \texttt{php artisan queue:work}.
    \item \textbf{Scheduler:} Add \texttt{* * * * * cd /var/www/smartshop && php artisan schedule:run >> /dev/null 2>&1} to crontab.
    \item \textbf{Optimization:} Run \texttt{php artisan config:cache}, \texttt{route:cache}, and \texttt{view:cache}.
\end{itemize}

